internal/page/extract.js, the script behind `winuse extract` on a Page, is
derived from these bladebro files at the commit above, and modified for
winuse:

- src/mcp/server/js/auto_extract.js: repeated-item detection, the item
  fields, the redirect unwrapping and the page's result count;
- src/adapters/js/jsonld.js: the schema.org JSON-LD reader;
- src/page/js/detect_block.js: the generic block-wall check (the
  site-specific branches and every solving step are left out).

What changed: the site adapters and site branches are gone; items group
loosely, sibling rows of one record merge, only the title link dedupes,
off-site links get no bonus, navs, footers, asides, prose and reference
lists never win, a weak list loses to JSON-LD, article pages have no list,
a single --root item gathers its siblings, data tables print cells by
header, more count formats are read, star counts are `stars`, and vote,
answer, view and comment counts are fields. The script runs in winuse's
isolated world, never the Page's own.
